  "method": "73 of the 507 surface-detector stations: the table sorted by x (west to east) and cut into 7 consecutive strips of 72 or 73 so that each record stays within 400 vertices; this strip covers x = -3.91 to -0.31 km from the CLF (station ids 0904 to 1204, id = column XX from the west and row YY from the south). Frame: TASDPosition.dat (TA Collaboration data release on Zenodo, DOI 10.5281/zenodo.8405760, licence CC BY 4.0) lists 507 stations as x, y, z in km; the release states neither origin nor orientation. Both were established here by registering the table against a published map: Fig. 5 of arXiv:2103.01086 is a vector plot on latitude and longitude axes of the 507 TA SDs; its 507 red markers, read from the vector graphic and calibrated on the axis ticks, were matched one-to-one to the table and fitted to it. With the origin at the Central Laser Facility, 39.296918 N 112.908733 W (arXiv:1410.3151 section 5.1), x pointing east and y north, the fitted rotation is -0.001 deg and scale 1.0004, the CLF falls at table (0.006, 0.005) km, and the median residual is 14 m (90th percentile 26 m, 99th percentile 40 m) after a 6 m mean shift. A UTM zone 12 grid would be rotated by about 1.2 deg here, so the axes are true east and north. Stations are placed with an ellipsoidal azimuthal-equidistant projection about the CLF (WGS 84; agrees with a tangent-plane ENU to under 1 m at 25 km; a spherical equirectangular conversion would differ by up to 60 m at the array corners and fits the figure worse). The z column is not used. Each station is a 1.73 m square, the area-equivalent of one 3 m2 scintillator layer (arXiv:1201.4964: \"Each layer of scintillator has an area of 3 m2\"), so a position marker with the scintillator's area, not its outline. Accuracy 100 m covers the registration scatter, the origin (about 10 m) and the choice of projection. Three stations differ from the figure by more than 100 m (1806: 443 m, 2212: 142 m, 1713: 133 m). In the table 1806 and 2212 sit 1.20 km from their grid neighbours while the figure position would break the square grid, so the figure is taken as the one in error; all three are drawn at their table position.",
  "name": "Telescope Array SD stations, strip 3 of 7 (west to east)",
  "notes": [
    "Checks done in the worklog: 507 stations (official 507); median nearest-neighbour distance 1.197 km (official square grid, 1.2 km spacing)."
  ],
